//www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/Psychedelic+Shack","lis":22230,"tags":["soul","motown","1970","funk","70s"],"wiki":"Psychedelic Shack is a 1970 album by The Temptations for the Gordy (Motown) label, which represents the Temptations' full-blown submergence into psychedelia. Completely written by Norman Whitfield and Barrett Strong and produced by Whitfield, Psychedelic Shack almost completely abandoned the \"Motown Sound\" formula for this LP; hard rock guitars, synthesizer sound effects, multitracked drums, sampling, and stereo-shifting vocals giving most of the album's songs a harder, less traditional feel than the Temptations' previous work. Background Psychedelic Shack was one of the last albums completed before the third incarnation of The Temptations (Dennis Edwards, Paul Williams, Eddie Kendricks, Melvin Franklin, and","lang":"en"},"The Temptations|Ball of Confusion (That’s What the World Is Today)":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/1c5f688596e949ccadb895afbde0a5ca.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/Ball+of+Confusion","lis":179,"tags":["soul","motown","70s","funk","rhythm and blues"]},"The Temptations|Take a Stroll Thru Your Mind":{"kind":"track","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/5b6bf241a8fe03aa0c50a9bcc9f0689a.png","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/_/Take+A+Stroll+Thru+Your+Mind","album":"Psychedelic Soul","lis":4983},"The Temptations|Slave":{"kind":"track","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/10d83c9ce261ab7ea51aabe59bc0f0d5.png","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/_/Slave","album":"The Best of the Temptations","lis":3924},"The Temptations|Puzzle People":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/43ad11831d4ded2bb9afa1d8b9b70b63.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/Puzzle+People","lis":50528,"tags":["soul","motown","funk","60s","1969"]},"The Temptations|All Directions":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/73d563378f6c799bcccd93956480aad4.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/All+Directions","lis":84230,"tags":["soul","1972","motown","70s","funk"],"wiki":"All Directions is a 1972 album by The Temptations for the Gordy (Motown) label, produced by Norman Whitfield. The LP features the #1 hit \"Papa Was a Rollin' Stone\", a twelve-minute cover of a Whitfield-produced Undisputed Truth single. \"Papa\" won three Grammy Awards in 1973: Best R&B Performance by a Group for the Temptations, Best R&B Instrumental Performance for Whitfield and arranger/conductor Paul Riser's instrumental version of \"Papa\" on the single's b-side, and Best R&B Song for Whitfield and lyricist Barrett Strong. All Directions was Strong's final LP as the Temptations' lyricist; Strong in fact had no direct involvement in","lang":"en"},"The Temptations|Just My Imagination (Running Away with Me)":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/fec7311fcce04407c427b05ccc99f580.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/Just+My+Imagination+(Running+Away+with+Me)","lis":233,"tags":["soul","motown","70s","oldies","mellow"]},"The Temptations|Papa Was a Rollin’ Stone":{"kind":"track","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/_/Papa+Was+A+Rollin%E2%80%99+Stone","album":"Now 100 Hits Legends","lis":971},"The Temptations|Runaway Child, Running Wild":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/2525586ca28d9be5744cf75f45e4d1d3.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Temptations/Runaway+Child,+Running+Wild","lis":105,"tags":["motown","soul","lab","the temptations","rhythm and blues"]},"The Temptations|Shakey Ground":{"kind":"album","img":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/133c54656e0645b7509ca840fd926a86.jpg","src":"lastfm","url":"